From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 01:48:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] kthread: export kthread_set_per_cpu()

A module that creates its own per-CPU kthreads with kthread_create_on_cpu()
and parks them across CPU hotplug needs kthread_set_per_cpu(): without
KTHREAD_IS_PER_CPU, kthread_unpark() does not rebind the thread when its
CPU comes back, and waking it while the CPU is online but not yet active
lets the scheduler move it to another CPU for good.

The Trusty driver is such a module: its nop threads must run on their
own CPU, since Trusty runs its work on the CPU that calls into it.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 kernel/kthread.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/kernel/kthread.c b/kernel/kthread.c
index a3f95c904..35afbff03 100644
--- a/kernel/kthread.c
+++ b/kernel/kthread.c
@@ -649,6 +649,7 @@ void kthread_set_per_cpu(struct task_struct *k, int cpu)
 	kthread->cpu = cpu;
 	set_bit(KTHREAD_IS_PER_CPU, &kthread->flags);
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(kthread_set_per_cpu);
 
 bool kthread_is_per_cpu(struct task_struct *p)
 {
